                'Plant geneticists have recently enhanced "stay-green" genes in <i>Sorghum bicolor</i> so leaves remain productive longer during severe seasonal droughts.',
                'Originally domesticated in northeastern Africa, <i>Sorghum bicolor</i> has a naturally deep root system.',
                'CRISPR gene editing is a recent laboratory technique applied by plant geneticists to modify specific crop genes.',
                'Using CRISPR gene editing, scientists are enhancing "stay-green" traits in sorghum—a hardy, deep-rooted African cereal grain that serves as a staple food across semi-arid regions—so its leaves stay productive longer during severe droughts.'
